1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,696
Shantanu Pawar: This is Project Flipbook. Type any star or coordinates, and it blinks real SPHEREx images to show what moves.

2
00:00:06,696 --> 00:00:13,335
Malhar Tamhankar: Every frame is a real SPHEREx file from NASA's IRSA archive, with its date and source shown on screen.

3
00:00:13,335 --> 00:00:20,464
Akhilesh Bhosale: SPHEREx sees different wavelengths across each image. We compare only matching ones, so colour change never looks like motion.

4
00:00:20,464 --> 00:00:27,618
Amrita Patil: We turn infrared into visible colour and measure each star's spectrum. Then export it all as a GIF or MP4.
